{"journal_version":1,"sequence":5,"replace_from":2,"message_count":3,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"We need answer verdict only first line exact. Need review diff without tools. Need assess regression. Need inspect given AsyncPanel partial. Need determine if any concrete issue. Key acceptance: success path unchanged never shows retry. error has Retry sync. Activating immediately returns loading then success after delay. Retry disappears after success cannot overlap timers repeated activation. Retry no reload/reset selected task. Preserve existing. Diff: initial useEffect reads query and schedules. Retry sets loading and schedules success. TimerRef clearing. Potential issue: scheduleResult callback uses timerRef; unmount cleanup effect depends on scheduleResult stable. Fine.\n\nPotential race: retry button sets state loading, scheduleResult clears existing timer. But in error state initial timer already fired and timerRef null. Fine.\n\nPotential issue with accessibility: role alert contains button; okay. Button class secondary existing style. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: The retry button is rendered only error branch; after success gone. Repeated activation: after clicking retry, state loading immediately and button disappears, so cannot click repeatedly unless state error again (it won't). If somehow click multiple before render? React event batching, the button unmounts; double click could trigger two events? scheduleResult clears timer. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: query string remains ?sync=error, but success after retry only state success. Since no re-initialization effect on state. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: Initial success at `/` now uses scheduleResult in effect. Equivalent delay 120. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: strict mode effect cleanup: In React StrictMode dev, effect runs setup, cleanup, setup. scheduleResult clears any previous. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: timerRef not cleared after cleanup? It sets null. Good.\n\nCould be issue that on retry, URL still has ?sync=error; but irrelevant.\n\nNeed assess \"Activating it immediately returns panel to Checking service…, then completes...\" setState loading in same event; yes.\n\n\"cannot create overlapping timers from repeated activation\": schedule clears pending. However retry action disappears immediately because state loading, so no repeat. fine.\n\nAny missing aria? Button named Retry sync. yes.\n\nNeed choose PASS likely.\n\nNeed first line exactly VERDICT: PASS. Then perhaps concise evidence. Ensure no markdown? It says first line exactly. Could provide short rationale. Since desired oververbosity 5 but budget. We can mention no concrete regression. Need not use tools. Need only final. Ensure first line exactly.","content":"VERDICT: PASS\n\nThe diff supports the acceptance criteria: the success path remains unchanged and renders no retry action; the error state includes a `Retry sync` button; retry sets `loading` immediately and schedules the same 120 ms success transition; the button disappears once success renders; `timerRef` clears any pending timer before scheduling and is cleaned up on unmount, preventing overlapping timers; and retry is local state only, so it does not reload or reset task selection. No concrete regression is supported by the supplied diff.","response_items":[{"id":"3deeb23b-39a7-45fe-9884-10ffcf01daf2","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need answer verdict only first line exact. Need review diff without tools. Need assess regression. Need inspect given AsyncPanel partial. Need determine if any concrete issue. Key acceptance: success path unchanged never shows retry. error has Retry sync. Activating immediately returns loading then success after delay. Retry disappears after success cannot overlap timers repeated activation. Retry no reload/reset selected task. Preserve existing. Diff: initial useEffect reads query and schedules. Retry sets loading and schedules success. TimerRef clearing. Potential issue: sche